Batch the smgr shim's store round trips.

zoureadv and zoustartreadv hand the whole block run to the Rust side
in one call so misses fan out across its thread pool, zouwritev pays
the WAL mirror barrier once on the newest LSN in the run instead of
once per page and passes skipFsync through so bulk fill pages buffer
in process, and registersync/immedsync settle those buffers through
zou_smgr_sync. Buffering only happens under a postmaster, bootstrap
and single user backends settle durability outside the smgr (initdb
fsyncs the data directory itself, which never holds relation pages
under zou), so they write eagerly. See crates/zou-pg/src/pending.rs
for the buffer's correctness argument.

